      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right that forcing a solution just to fill the silence adds more noise to an already quiet and painful place. It is incredibly brave and honest to question if the suffering is even temporary or if it is simply who you have become after building this wall; often, that feeling of being \"unfixable\" is actually the symptom of deep exhaustion rather than an unchangeable truth. While the desire to just wait for the end is powerful, even finding one small moment of relief from the constant heaviness, like stepping outside alone or sitting by a window, can gently remind you that your thoughts and current state are not permanent facts.",
